{
  "id": "ep069",
  "duration": 55.662,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.525,
      "text": "A spacecraft designed to die in thirty-two minutes lasted two hours.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Venera 9 Space Probe 01.jpg",
        "credit": "Stolbovsky",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Venera_9_Space_Probe_01.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 1.7,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 1.7,
          "end": 4.533,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.525,
      "end": 11.92,
      "text": "On March 1, 1982, the Soviet Union's Venera 13 lander descended through the clouds of Venus.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "PIA23791-Venus-RealAndEnhancedContrastViews-20200608 (cropped).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL-Caltech",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PIA23791-Venus-RealAndEnhancedContrastViews-20200608_(cropped).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.533,
          "end": 11.933,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 11.92,
      "end": 20.715,
      "text": "The probe touched down near Phoebe Regio, facing ninety atmospheres of pressure and temperatures around four hundred sixty degrees Celsius.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "2438 pioneer venus map of venus.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/Ames/U.S. Geological Survey/Massachusetts Institute of Technology",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2438_pioneer_venus_map_of_venus.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 11.933,
          "end": 20.7,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 20.715,
      "end": 27.66,
      "text": "Safe inside its armored hull, Venera 13 drilled into the rocky ground to analyze a soil sample.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "2438 pioneer venus map of venus.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/Ames/U.S. Geological Survey/Massachusetts Institute of Technology",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2438_pioneer_venus_map_of_venus.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 20.7,
          "end": 27.667,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 27.66,
      "end": 34.68,
      "text": "It also captured and transmitted the first color photographs ever taken from the surface of another planet.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "V13 vg261 262.tif",
        "credit": "USSR/NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:V13_vg261_262.tif"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 27.667,
          "end": 34.667,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 34.68,
      "end": 41.25,
      "text": "Decades later, a Russian scientist claimed these photos showed moving alien life, like a scorpion.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Surface of Venus from Venera 13.jpg",
        "credit": "Lunar and Planetary Institute from Houston, TX, USA",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Surface_of_Venus_from_Venera_13.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 34.667,
          "end": 41.267,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 41.25,
      "end": 48.1,
      "text": "But experts proved the mysterious alien was actually just the lander's discarded camera lens cap.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 41.267,
          "end": 48.1,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 48.1,
      "end": 55.312,
      "text": "In 1982, Soviet engineers celebrated as this historic machine defied its death sentence on Venus.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Venera 9 Space Probe 01.jpg",
        "credit": "Stolbovsky",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Venera_9_Space_Probe_01.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 48.1,
          "end": 55.667,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
